{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966791,"nonce":"Oh4hfY8NxhkAtKh1lQ28EU0NAio=","title":"apply_binding_deltas only set visible_anim_active=true, never cleared, so once the walker","message":"The compositor fast path's `apply_binding_deltas` (in [context.rs](crates/blinc_app/src/context.rs)) used to only ever *set* `visible_anim_active=true` when a binding was active — it never wrote `false`. The full-paint walker resets the flag to `false` at the top of every `render_with_motion`; the fast path skips the walker. So once the walker raised the flag during the spring-animating frames, every subsequent fast-path frame left it at `true` even after the spring settled. Phase 5's `needs_animation_redraw = needs_animation_redraw_raw \u0026\u0026 visible_anim` then stayed true forever, the chain kept calling `request_redraw`, and the user saw \"30 % CPU since interaction and never drops.\"\n\n**Why:** The original posture (\"only set, never clear\") was defensive — visible_anim_active is also written by Canvas / motion-FSM paths, and the author didn't want fast-path runs to stomp on what those set. But on the fast path the gate already requires no rebuild / no relayout / no CSS / no scroll — so the only remaining dynamic source is motion bindings, which apply_binding_deltas already tracks. Canvas / motion-FSM paths drive separate signals (`needs_motion_redraw`, `has_visible_animating_statefuls`), so clearing visible_anim_active when nothing is binding-active is safe.\n\n**How to apply:** When writing to a flag that another path also writes, decide whether your write is authoritative for your code path. If the other path has its own redraw signal you don't need to preserve their `true`, write your observation directly:\n\n```rust\ntree.set_visible_anim_active(any_binding_active);\n```\n\ninstead of:\n\n```rust\nif any_binding_active {\n    tree.set_visible_anim_active(true);\n}\n// stale `true` from previous full paint stays latched\n```\n\nSame shape to watch for in any fast-path / incremental-update code that bypasses a \"full reset\" pass.\n\nSee also [[gotcha-scrollbar-spring-spin]].","files":null}]}